---
import ReferenceMap from "../ReferenceMap.astro";
import RecapPhotos from "./RecapPhotos.astro";
---

<div class="event-recap" data-event-recap>
  <section class="recap-hero" aria-labelledby="recap-title">
    <div class="container recap-hero__inner">
      <div class="recap-hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Activate All RI 2026 · September 11–13</p>
        <h1 id="recap-title"><span>We did it!!</span> <span>Thank you!!</span></h1>
        <p class="recap-hero__thanks">Together, we put Rhode Island on the air. Thank you to every activator who packed the gear, every hunter who called back, and everyone who helped make the weekend happen.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button" data-variant="primary" href="#weekend-results">Explore the results</a>
          <a class="button" data-variant="light" href="/activate-ri-2026/media/">Photos</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="recap-hero__map">
        <ReferenceMap id="activate-ri-recap-map" variant="coverage" resultsMode recapMode
          title="Rhode Island park activity during Activate All RI 2026" caption=""
          legendPlacement="below" legendTitle="2026 park activity" showBoundaries={false} />
        <p class="recap-map-caption" data-recap-coverage>Explore the parks that brought us together.</p>
        <a href="/activate-ri-2026/parks/">See each park’s results <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="recap-results container" id="weekend-results" aria-labelledby="recap-results-title">
    <div class="recap-section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The weekend in numbers</p><h2 id="recap-results-title">Look what we did together.</h2></div>
      <p class="recap-status" data-recap-status role="status">Loading the latest event results…</p>
    </div>
    <dl class="recap-stats" aria-label="Provisional event results">
      <div><dt>Parks confirmed</dt><dd data-recap-stat="parks">—</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Qualifying activations</dt><dd data-recap-stat="activations">—</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Activator callsigns</dt><dd data-recap-stat="callsigns">—</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Logged QSO credits</dt><dd data-recap-stat="qsos">—</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="recap-results-note">Logs are still coming in, so these results are provisional. Early activations on September 10 are included.</p>
    <details class="recap-method">
      <summary>About these numbers</summary>
      <p>A park is confirmed when its POTA history includes an event activation with at least 10 QSOs. Recorded activity without a qualifying log is shown separately on the map.</p>
      <p>Activations count each park, callsign, and UTC date separately. Callsigns come from uploaded logs and can represent an individual or a group. QSO credits include all recorded event logs, including attempts with fewer than 10 contacts. A contact made at several parks can earn several park credits, so this is not a count of unique contacts.</p>
      <p>Results cover September 10–13, 2026, in UTC. Official <a href="https://pota.app/">Parks on the Air records</a> remain the source of truth for logs and awards.</p>
    </details>
    <div class="recap-modes" data-recap-modes hidden>
      <div class="recap-modes__heading"><h3>A little of everything on the bands.</h3><span>Logged QSO credits by mode</span></div>
      <div class="recap-modes__bar" aria-hidden="true"><span data-recap-mode-bar="phone"></span><span data-recap-mode-bar="cw"></span><span data-recap-mode-bar="data"></span></div>
      <dl class="recap-modes__labels">
        <div><dt><span class="recap-mode-dot" data-mode="phone" aria-hidden="true"></span>Phone</dt><dd data-recap-mode="phone"></dd></div>
        <div><dt><span class="recap-mode-dot" data-mode="cw" aria-hidden="true"></span>CW</dt><dd data-recap-mode="cw"></dd></div>
        <div><dt><span class="recap-mode-dot" data-mode="data" aria-hidden="true"></span>Data</dt><dd data-recap-mode="data"></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <noscript><p><a href="/activate-ri-2026/parks/">Open park results</a>. Detailed results and the map need JavaScript; the photos, thank-you, and event links are still here.</p></noscript>
  </section>

  <RecapPhotos />

  <section class="recap-thanks container" aria-labelledby="recap-thanks-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Both ends of the contact</p>
    <h2 id="recap-thanks-title">It took all of us.</h2>
    <div class="recap-thanks__pair">
      <article><h3>To our activators</h3><p>Thank you for packing the gear, making the trip, finding a place to set up, and putting the parks on the air. Whether you made one stop or a whole rove, you gave hunters a reason to listen for Rhode Island.</p></article>
      <article><h3>To our hunters</h3><p>Thank you for listening, calling back, and helping fill the logs. Whether you were chasing one last park or just stopped by for a contact, you helped make this weekend happen. Every contact needed someone at the other end.</p></article>
    </div>
    <p class="recap-thanks__helpers">And to everyone who helped organize, shared an update or a photo, or lent a hand along the way: thank you for taking care of the people behind the callsigns.</p>
    <details class="recap-roll" data-recap-roll hidden><summary>Activator callsigns in the logs</summary><p data-recap-callsigns></p><p class="recap-roll__note">This list grows as logs arrive. Our thanks go just as much to the hunters and helpers who aren’t listed here.</p></details>
  </section>

  <section class="recap-keep-going" aria-labelledby="recap-community-title">
    <div class="container recap-keep-going__inner">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Keep in touch</p><h2 id="recap-community-title">There’s always more radio to talk about.</h2><p>Share a photo, swap a story, or keep up with the RI POTA community. Any news about another Activate All RI will be shared once the organizers have decided.</p><a class="button" data-variant="primary" href="https://groups.io/g/RI-POTA">Join the RI POTA conversation</a></div>
      <nav class="recap-wrapup" aria-label="2026 event resources">
        <h3>Your 2026 event links</h3>
        <a href="/activate-ri-2026/activator/media/">Share your photos <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href="/activate-ri-2026/schedule/">Browse the 2026 schedule <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href="/activate-ri-2026/help/">Send a correction or get help <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        <a href="/activate-ri-2026/activator/">Activator access <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  import { subscribeEventPhase } from "../../lib/activate-ri/event-phase";
  import { potaParkStatusStore } from "../../lib/activate-ri/pota-status-store";
  import { summarizeRecap } from "../../lib/activate-ri/recap";
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-event-recap]");
  if (root) {
    const format = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US");
    const setText = (selector: string, value: string) => { const element = root.querySelector(selector); if (element) element.textContent = value; };
    let started = false;
    subscribeEventPhase((phase) => {
      if (phase !== "post-event" || started) return;
      started = true;
      potaParkStatusStore.subscribe((state) => {
        root.dataset.resultsState = state.status;
        if (state.status !== "ready") {
          if (state.status === "unavailable") setText("[data-recap-status]", "Results are temporarily unavailable. Please try again in a little while.");
          return;
        }
        const { snapshot, refreshFailed } = state;
        const stats = summarizeRecap(snapshot);
        setText('[data-recap-stat="parks"]', `${format.format(stats.confirmedParks)} / ${format.format(stats.totalParks)}`);
        setText('[data-recap-stat="activations"]', format.format(stats.activationCount));
        setText('[data-recap-stat="callsigns"]', format.format(stats.callsigns.length));
        setText('[data-recap-stat="qsos"]', format.format(stats.qsoCredits));
        const checkedAt = snapshot.lastPotaSyncAt ? new Date(snapshot.lastPotaSyncAt) : null;
        const timestamp = checkedAt && Number.isFinite(checkedAt.valueOf())
          ? `POTA logs checked ${new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", { month: "short", day: "numeric", year: "numeric", hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit", timeZone: "America/New_York", timeZoneName: "short" }).format(checkedAt)}.`
          : "Waiting for a completed POTA log check.";
        const warning = refreshFailed ? "The latest refresh failed; showing the last available results."
          : snapshot.warning ?? (snapshot.stale ? "The latest log check is delayed." : "");
        setText("[data-recap-status]", `${timestamp}${warning ? ` ${warning}` : ""}`);
        const activity = stats.confirmedParks + stats.observedParks;
        setText("[data-recap-coverage]", activity > 0
          ? `${activity === stats.totalParks ? `Activity recorded at all ${format.format(stats.totalParks)} parks.` : `Activity recorded at ${format.format(activity)} of ${format.format(stats.totalParks)} parks.`}${stats.observedParks ? ` ${format.format(stats.observedParks)} ${stats.observedParks === 1 ? "park doesn’t" : "parks don’t"} have a qualifying log yet.` : ""}`
          : "The map will fill in as event activity is recorded.");
        const modeTotal = stats.modes.phone + stats.modes.cw + stats.modes.data;
        root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-recap-modes]")!.hidden = modeTotal === 0;
        for (const mode of ["phone", "cw", "data"] as const) {
          setText(`[data-recap-mode="${mode}"]`, format.format(stats.modes[mode]));
          root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-recap-mode-bar="${mode}"]`)!.style.width = `${modeTotal ? stats.modes[mode] / modeTotal * 100 : 0}%`;
        }
        setText("[data-recap-callsigns]", stats.callsigns.join(" · "));
        root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-recap-roll]")!.hidden = stats.callsigns.length === 0;
      });
      potaParkStatusStore.start();
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .event-recap { --recap-phone: #277a70; --recap-cw: #b67a37; --recap-data: #526bb3; }
  .recap-hero { background: #18312f; color: #f7f4ed; padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); }
  .recap-hero__inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr; align-items: center; gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem); }
  .recap-hero .eyebrow { color: #e9bc7e; font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .12em; }
  .recap-hero h1 { color: #fffaf0; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 4.6vw, 4.5rem); max-width: 15ch; line-height: 1.05; text-wrap: balance; }
  .recap-hero h1 > span { display: block; }
  .recap-hero h1 > span:last-child { color: #edc18a; }
  .recap-hero__thanks { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.6vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.55; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .recap-hero__copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 47ch; }
  .recap-hero .button-row { margin-top: 1.7rem; }
  .recap-hero .button[data-variant="primary"] { background: #edc18a; color: #18312f; border-color: #edc18a; }
  .recap-hero .button[data-variant="light"] { background: transparent; color: #fffaf0; border-color: #a4b4a6; }
  .recap-hero a:hover { color: #edc18a; }
  .recap-hero .button:hover { background: #fffaf0; color: #18312f; }
  .recap-hero__map { min-width: 0; }
  .recap-hero__map :global(.map-preview) { margin: 0; height: auto; min-height: 0; box-shadow: none; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #f7f4ed; }
  .recap-hero__map :global(.ri-reference-map) { height: 370px; min-height: 0; }
  .recap-hero__map :global(.map-legend--below) { color: #18312f; background: #f7f4ed; padding: .8rem 1rem; margin: 0; }
  .recap-map-caption { margin: .9rem 0 .35rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .recap-hero__map > a { font-size: .9rem; color: #edc18a; }
  .recap-results { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .recap-section-heading { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; }
  .recap-section-heading h2, .recap-thanks h2, .recap-keep-going h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.9rem); line-height: 1.1; }
  .recap-status { max-width: 35ch; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0; }
  .recap-stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin: 2rem 0 1rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); padding-block: 1.5rem; }
  .recap-stats > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; justify-content: end; gap: .7rem; padding-inline: 1.5rem; border-left: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }
  .recap-stats > div:first-child { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }
  .recap-stats dt { font-size: .86rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .recap-stats dd { margin: 0; color: var(--surface-ink); font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 4vw, 3.8rem); line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .recap-results-note { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: .87rem; }
  .recap-method { font-size: .85rem; max-width: 85ch; }
  .recap-method summary, .recap-roll summary { cursor: pointer; width: fit-content; color: var(--link-strong); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .2em; }
  .recap-method p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .recap-modes { margin-top: 2.2rem; max-width: 750px; }
  .recap-modes__heading { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .recap-modes h3 { font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .recap-modes__heading > span { font-size: .75rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .recap-modes__bar { display: flex; height: 12px; overflow: hidden; border-radius: 3px; margin-top: 1rem; }
  [data-recap-mode-bar="phone"], [data-mode="phone"] { background: var(--recap-phone); }
  [data-recap-mode-bar="cw"], [data-mode="cw"] { background: var(--recap-cw); }
  [data-recap-mode-bar="data"], [data-mode="data"] { background: var(--recap-data); }
  .recap-modes__labels, .recap-modes__labels > div, .recap-modes dt { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .recap-modes__labels { gap: .8rem 1.7rem; margin: .75rem 0 0; font-size: .82rem; }
  .recap-modes__labels > div { gap: .5rem; }
  .recap-modes dd { margin: 0; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .recap-modes dt { gap: .35rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .recap-mode-dot { width: .6rem; height: .6rem; border-radius: 50%; }
  .recap-thanks { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); }
  .recap-thanks__pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .recap-thanks h3 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
  .recap-thanks p { line-height: 1.75; }
  .recap-thanks__helpers { max-width: 80ch; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .recap-roll { margin-top: 1.7rem; padding-top: 1.4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); }
  [data-recap-callsigns] { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; word-spacing: .3rem; }
  .recap-roll__note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 85ch; }
  .recap-keep-going { background: var(--notice-surface); padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .recap-keep-going__inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr; gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); }
  .recap-keep-going h2 { max-width: 20ch; text-wrap: balance; }
  .recap-keep-going p { line-height: 1.7; }
  .recap-keep-going .button { margin-top: .5rem; }
  .recap-wrapup { display: grid; align-content: start; }
  .recap-wrapup h3 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin-bottom: .7rem; }
  .recap-wrapup a { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding-block: .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); color: var(--link-strong); font-size: .9rem; }
  @media (max-width: 850px) {
    .recap-hero__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .recap-hero h1 { max-width: 20ch; }
    .recap-hero__copy > p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 60ch; }
    .recap-hero__map :global(.ri-reference-map) { height: 330px; }
    .recap-section-heading { display: block; }
    .recap-status { margin-top: 1rem; max-width: none; }
    .recap-stats > div { padding-inline: .9rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .recap-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem 0; }
    .recap-stats > div:nth-child(3) { border-left: 0; padding-left: 0; }
    .recap-stats dd { font-size: 2.65rem; }
    .recap-thanks__pair, .recap-keep-going__inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .recap-thanks__pair { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .recap-hero .button-row { align-items: stretch; }
  }
</style>
